From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:11:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Alt shade shortcuts for keyboards without Fn

The keyboard-first shade design uses Fn+Down (open, then expand Quick
Settings), Fn+Up (one level back) and Menu / Fn+Enter (row actions).
The Q25 keyboard has Alt, Shift, Sym and letters but no Fn, and
LineageOS keeps the Menu key for its own key actions, so:

* Alt+Down (trackpad or D-pad of the same keyboard) becomes the system
  navigation Down key in PhoneWindowManager. SystemUI already turns it
  into "open the shade; if open, expand Quick Settings". Only Alt may
  be held, software keyboards never trigger it, and it is not taken on
  the keyguard or before setup (SystemUI ignores it there). Pure
  policy: policy/sable/SableShadeKeys.java.
* Alt+Up, handled pre-IME by the shade window only (so apps keep it),
  steps back one level exactly like Back: Quick Settings to
  notifications, then closed.
* Alt+Enter on a focused notification row opens the row's actions
  menu (the long-press menu). Its release is swallowed so that letting
  go of Alt first never opens the notification. Text input still wins
  and Alt+letters stay plain keys.
